d circumnavigation. On this voyage, Captain Cook discovered islands and peoples, while Georg Forster focused on animals and plants, discovering more than 400 species that had been unknown to Europeans until then. “Terra X” follows German actor Robert Atzorn on his search for traces around the world. He gets to know a young man, whose philosophy and conception of the world still appear to be really modern. Sophisticated dramatic reconstructions bring the fateful sea journey to life. The film portrays a great natural scientist whose knowledge and legacy determined patterns for scientific research in the 21st century.","duration":3000000,"originalContentDuration":2610000,"allotment":3000,"rating":"9+","featuredImage":{"path":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f85ed73a0a1001450b28f/screenshot16_9_1786058642344.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=540&q=75&w=960"},"genre":"Documentary","type":"movie","seasonsNumbers":[],"stitched":{"path":"/stitch/hls/episode/626f85ed73a0a1001450b28f/master.m3u8"},"covers":[{"aspectRatio":"347:500","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f85ed73a0a1001450b28f/poster_1786058642344.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=1000&q=75&w=694"},{"aspectRatio":"4:3","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f85ed73a0a1001450b28f/screenshot4_3_1786058642344.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=480&q=75&w=640"},{"aspectRatio":"16:9","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f85ed73a0a1001450b28f/screenshot16_9_1786058642344.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=540&q=75&w=960"}],"categories":[{"id":"5b8d6316aff98879a8ee7157"}],"poster16_9":{"path":"https://images.pluto.tv/assets/images/default/vod.screenshot16_9-default.jpg"},"clip":{"directors":["Tom Ockers","Frank Vorpahl"],"writers":["Tom Ockers","Frank Vorpahl"],"producers":["Susanne Stenner","Ulrich Lenze"],"originalReleaseDate":"2012-05-28T00:00:00Z"},"avail":{},"stream_url":"https://cfd-v4-service-channel-stitcher-use1-1.prd.pluto.tv/v2/stitch/hls/episode/626f85ed73a0a1001450b28f/master.m3u8?advertisingId=&appName=web&appVersion=7.9.0-a9cca6b89aea4dc0998b92a51989d2adb9a9025d&app_name=web&clientDeviceType=0&clientID=688e2fcf-3b1e-4478-a146-7d2b26ed9b90&clientModelNumber=1.0.0&country=GB&deviceDNT=false&deviceId=688e2fcf-3b1e-4478-a146-7d2b26ed9b90&deviceLat=51.5100&deviceLon=-0.0800&deviceMake=Chrome&deviceModel=web&deviceType=web&deviceVersion=16.2.0&marketingRegion=GB&serverSideAds=true&sessionID=04ec44b2-d506-11f1-9e7f-2af1ca94ebdb&sid=04ec44b2-d506-11f1-9e7f-2af1ca94ebdb&userId=&jwt=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsImtpZCI6IjU3MGE4NTE5LTNhNzEtNGQ1Ni1iMTAyLTIwN2Q4MjI4MTZkYiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..12EU-uv7NlsyswTGY3ySL8nLtjjLm4qOFCmlC5Bnkno&masterJWTPassthrough=true"},"626f85a073a0a10014505eba-uk":{"_id":"626f85a073a0a10014505eba","seriesID":"626f859e73a0a10014505eb3","slug":"wild-sex-2019-1-1","name":"Wild Sex","summary":"Sex is at the heart of everything, driving touching courtships and fierce battles, it can change an animals purpose and persona. This is the story of how wild things get sexy.","description":"Sex is at the heart of everything. It’s the only real way of leaving a legacy - in the genes of the future. But there’s more than just the act - it’s the build up to it when wildlife shows its incredible diversity. It drives touching courtships and fierce battles. Hormones and sex drive are forces that shape behaviour and can change an animal’s purpose and persona. This is the story of how wild things get sexy. Without sex, there’s nothing. It’s a driving force throughout nature. The act of sex is mostly to make babies, but let’s face it, its foreplay that really counts - it brings out the best and the worst in the animal kingdom. Pre-coital courtship can give pleasure, but also gives the participants the chance to check each other out and make sure they’ve found the perfect match. It affects us all. Birds do it, bees do it, all the way through the animals kingdom. From fire flies who mix up their own chemistry sets to fill the forest with mood lighting, to mayflies that emerge on mass, by the millions to mate. Their vast orgies attract predators of all sizes. Fish risk their lives climbing rivers from the sea, and a barrage of bears and other predators - just for sex - but the mission is so strenuous it kills them, as soon as their eggs are laid, they wither and die. Sex and the hormones that drive it can turn cute and cuddly into a sex beast. It turns out the koala is a sex maniac, more into rape than romance. Many mammals, from guanaco (wild llama) to hippos chase, wrestle and bite their way to a romantic interlude. Huge male red Kangaroos even box. When it comes to wild sex, mammals are amazing, but its birds that are the real show stoppers. From dazzling peacocks to booming bustards, fighting turkeys to dancing birds of paradise, birds go all out on foreplay - though you sometimes have to wonder if it’s worth it - after all that parading their sex is over in seconds; There’s a lot of effort for very little reward.","duration":3480000,"originalContentDuration":3015000,"allotment":3480,"rating":"12+","featuredImage":{"path":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f85a073a0a10014505eba/screenshot16_9_1787770442076.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=540&q=75&w=960"},"genre":"Documentary","type":"movie","seasonsNumbers":[],"stitched":{"path":"/stitch/hls/episode/626f85a073a0a10014505eba/master.m3u8"},"covers":[{"aspectRatio":"347:500","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f85a073a0a10014505eba/poster_1787770442076.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=1000&q=75&w=694"},{"aspectRatio":"4:3","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f85a073a0a10014505eba/screenshot4_3_1787770442076.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=480&q=75&w=640"},{"aspectRatio":"16:9","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f85a073a0a10014505eba/screenshot16_9_1787770442076.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=540&q=75&w=960"}],"categories":[{"id":"5b8d6316aff98879a8ee7157"}],"poster16_9":{"path":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f85a073a0a10014505eba/poster16_9_1787770442077.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=540&q=75&w=960"},"clip":{"actors":["Andy Wisher"],"directors":["Tom Synnatzschke","Phil Coles"],"producers":["Tom Synnatzschke","Phil Coles"],"originalReleaseDate":"2019-01-29T00:00:00Z"},"avail":{},"stream_url":"https://cfd-v4-service-channel-stitcher-use1-1.prd.pluto.tv/v2/stitch/hls/episode/626f85a073a0a10014505eba/master.m3u8?advertisingId=&appName=web&appVersion=7.9.0-a9cca6b89aea4dc0998b92a51989d2adb9a9025d&app_name=web&clientDeviceType=0&clientID=688e2fcf-3b1e-4478-a146-7d2b26ed9b90&clientModelNumber=1.0.0&country=GB&deviceDNT=false&deviceId=688e2fcf-3b1e-4478-a146-7d2b26ed9b90&deviceLat=51.5100&deviceLon=-0.0800&deviceMake=Chrome&deviceModel=web&deviceType=web&deviceVersion=16.2.0&marketingRegion=GB&serverSideAds=true&sessionID=04ec44b2-d506-11f1-9e7f-2af1ca94ebdb&sid=04ec44b2-d506-11f1-9e7f-2af1ca94ebdb&userId=&jwt=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsImtpZCI6IjU3MGE4NTE5LTNhNzEtNGQ1Ni1iMTAyLTIwN2Q4MjI4MTZkYiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..12EU-uv7NlsyswTGY3ySL8nLtjjLm4qOFCmlC5Bnkno&masterJWTPassthrough=true"},"626f859473a0a10014504f31-uk":{"_id":"626f859473a0a10014504f31","seriesID":"626f859273a0a10014504f2a","slug":"wild-serbia-2013-1-1","name":"Wild Serbia","summary":"Serbia, in the heart of the Balkans, is one of Europe’s little natural wonders.","description":"Serbia is in the heart of the Balkans, a “little Europe“ within Europe; with its rich variety of landscapes and natural beauties, it certainly does this name justice. This nature documentary presents Serbia's breath-taking, picturesque regions and unique wildlife on a journey to the most beautiful and wildest areas of the Balkan peninsula, from high mountains across gentle hills to the vast plains of the Puszta. Serbia is only about five times the size of Schleswig Holstein, yet here the most varied vegetation zones, animal kingdoms and cultures meet. And even today a large number of Serbian people live in close communion with nature. They are proud of the storks’ nests in the villages, the ancient species of livestock that have been preserved and the vultures that return to make their home here. In many places people are pleased to see bears, lynx and wolves, and even jackals are at home in the forests of Siberia. It is a country full of traditions and folklore, with deep influences from the Orient as well as the West. The Danube is the most prominent river in Serbia. As it makes its way through the Carpathian Mountains of Rumania it forms the most imposing gorge in Europe, the Iron Gates. Other striking features of Serbia's landscape include the archaic earth pyramids of Devil's Town, towering up in powerful red colours - and what must be the driest region of Siberia, the Deliblatska Pescara, which is also known as Europe's Sahara. Colourful birds called bee-eaters have settled on a rocky slope - a whole, noisy colony of them. They make their nests in caves which they dig themselves in the ground, and the inaccessible location means it is difficult for enemies to reach them. The more frequently the male brings the female insects it has caught, the more powerful is the bond between them later.","duration":3420000,"originalContentDuration":2925000,"allotment":3420,"rating":"All","featuredImage":{"path":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f859473a0a10014504f31/screenshot16_9_1787770805507.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=540&q=75&w=960"},"genre":"Documentary","type":"movie","seasonsNumbers":[],"stitched":{"path":"/stitch/hls/episode/626f859473a0a10014504f31/master.m3u8"},"covers":[{"aspectRatio":"347:500","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f859473a0a10014504f31/poster_1787770809144.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=1000&q=75&w=694"},{"aspectRatio":"4:3","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f859473a0a10014504f31/screenshot4_3_1787770805507.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=480&q=75&w=640"},{"aspectRatio":"16:9","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f859473a0a10014504f31/screenshot16_9_1787770805507.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=540&q=75&w=960"}],"categories":[{"id":"5b8d6316aff98879a8ee7157"}],"poster16_9":{"path":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f859473a0a10014504f31/poster16_9_1787770809144.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=540&q=75&w=960"},"clip":{"actors":["Rob Quirk"],"directors":["Marion Pöllmann","Rainer Bergomaz","Rob Quirk"],"writers":["Marion Pöllmann","Rainer Bergomaz","Rob Quirk"],"producers":["Susanne Lummer","Jörn Röver"],"originalReleaseDate":"2013-12-27T00:00:00Z"},"avail":{},"stream_url":"https://cfd-v4-service-channel-stitcher-use1-1.prd.pluto.tv/v2/stitch/hls/episode/626f859473a0a10014504f31/master.m3u8?advertisingId=&appName=web&appVersion=7.9.0-a9cca6b89aea4dc0998b92a51989d2adb9a9025d&app_name=web&clientDeviceType=0&clientID=688e2fcf-3b1e-4478-a146-7d2b26ed9b90&clientModelNumber=1.0.0&country=GB&deviceDNT=false&deviceId=688e2fcf-3b1e-4478-a146-7d2b26ed9b90&deviceLat=51.5100&deviceLon=-0.0800&deviceMake=Chrome&deviceModel=web&deviceType=web&deviceVersion=16.2.0&marketingRegion=GB&serverSideAds=true&sessionID=04ec44b2-d506-11f1-9e7f-2af1ca94ebdb&sid=04ec44b2-d506-11f1-9e7f-2af1ca94ebdb&userId=&jwt=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsImtpZCI6IjU3MGE4NTE5LTNhNzEtNGQ1Ni1iMTAyLTIwN2Q4MjI4MTZkYiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..12EU-uv7NlsyswTGY3ySL8nLtjjLm4qOFCmlC5Bnkno&masterJWTPassthrough=true"},"626f859773a0a100145052d7-uk":{"_id":"626f859773a0a100145052d7","seriesID":"626f859573a0a100145052d0","slug":"wild-poland-2011-1-1","name":"Wild Poland","summary":"From “Polands Amazonia” between Biebrza and Narew up to the mountains of the Tatra and into “Polands desert” close the Baltic Sea: “Wild Poland” is full of natural wonders.","description":"Where in Europe are bisons still to be found in the wild? And where do probably more migratory birds breed than in any other European country? The flora and fauna of Poland are full of surprises: the South is dominated by the 2000m peaks of the Tatra, to the North-East the Biebrza river forms one of the largest swamp regions of Europe, a paradise for rare birds like the ruff. Masuria is the breeding-ground for thousands of white storks, more than anywhere else on Earth. The much shier and rarer black stork also finds refuge in the large expanses of forest that stretch to the Baltic Sea. In winter, an icy wind sweeps Eastern Poland and only those with a thick skin survive in the region bordering Belorus. The cold doesn’t bother the bison. Thick coats protect these ancient cattle against the snow and icy wind, but lack of food in winter does present a problem. The bison here are among the last of their kind. Once upon a time, huge herds roamed most of the European continent, today the only bison in Central Europe living in the wild are located in Eastern Poland. Poland’s hard winters are no problem for otter and beaver, whose extremely dense coats protect them against the cold and enable them to swim and dive in the icy water. Although both animals are water-dwellers, they’re not rivals: beavers are vegetarians and in winter eat stores of leaves and bark. Otters are active hunters all year round and live on fish and crabs. As soon as spring arrives in Poland, the river Biebrza becomes a hive of activity: thousands of birds vie with each other to be heard as they use the vast area of swampland to rest and breed. White-winged black terns and black-necked grebes build their nests, then the mating season begins for the ruffs, with the males strutting their stuff for potential mates.","duration":3360000,"originalContentDuration":2895000,"allotment":3360,"rating":"All","featuredImage":{"path":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f859773a0a100145052d7/screenshot16_9_1787770805335.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=540&q=75&w=960"},"genre":"Documentary","type":"movie","seasonsNumbers":[],"stitched":{"path":"/stitch/hls/episode/626f859773a0a100145052d7/master.m3u8"},"covers":[{"aspectRatio":"347:500","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f859773a0a100145052d7/poster_1787770805335.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=1000&q=75&w=694"},{"aspectRatio":"4:3","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f859773a0a100145052d7/screenshot4_3_1787770805335.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=480&q=75&w=640"},{"aspectRatio":"16:9","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f859773a0a100145052d7/screenshot16_9_1787770805335.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=540&q=75&w=960"}],"categories":[{"id":"5b8d6316aff98879a8ee7157"}],"poster16_9":{"path":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f859773a0a100145052d7/poster16_9_1787770805335.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=540&q=75&w=960"},"clip":{"actors":["Rob Quirk"],"directors":["Hans-Peter Kuttler","Ernst Sasse"],"writers":["Hans-Peter Kuttler","Ernst Sasse","Rob Quirk"],"producers":["Susanne Lummer"],"originalReleaseDate":"2011-12-31T00:00:00Z"},"avail":{},"stream_url":"https://cfd-v4-service-channel-stitcher-use1-1.prd.pluto.tv/v2/stitch/hls/episode/626f859773a0a100145052d7/master.m3u8?advertisingId=&appName=web&appVersion=7.9.0-a9cca6b89aea4dc0998b92a51989d2adb9a9025d&app_name=web&clientDeviceType=0&clientID=688e2fcf-3b1e-4478-a146-7d2b26ed9b90&clientModelNumber=1.0.0&country=GB&deviceDNT=false&deviceId=688e2fcf-3b1e-4478-a146-7d2b26ed9b90&deviceLat=51.5100&deviceLon=-0.0800&deviceMake=Chrome&deviceModel=web&deviceType=web&deviceVersion=16.2.0&marketingRegion=GB&serverSideAds=true&sessionID=04ec44b2-d506-11f1-9e7f-2af1ca94ebdb&sid=04ec44b2-d506-11f1-9e7f-2af1ca94ebdb&userId=&jwt=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsImtpZCI6IjU3MGE4NTE5LTNhNzEtNGQ1Ni1iMTAyLTIwN2Q4MjI4MTZkYiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..12EU-uv7NlsyswTGY3ySL8nLtjjLm4qOFCmlC5Bnkno&masterJWTPassthrough=true"},"626f859073a0a10014504ade-uk":{"_id":"626f859073a0a10014504ade","seriesID":"626f858f73a0a10014504ad7","slug":"wild-hungary-a-water-wonderland-2010-1-1","name":"Wild Hungary - A Water Wonderland","summary":"Wild Hungary - A Water Wonderland is a wildlife documentary about a white-tailed eagle family, a young otter and a giant catfish that share the wetlands of this country in Europe.","description":"\"Wild Hungary - A Water Wonderland\" is a wildlife documentary about a white-tailed eagle family, a young otter and a giant catfish that share the wetlands of this country in Central Europe. Hungary lies in the bottom of the huge Pannonian Basin encircled by the peaks of the Alps and the Carpathians. Countless rivers and streams run from the mountains into the heart of the basin like the Danube or the Tisza and the countryside is densely scattered with thousands of lakes as well. In such a water paradise it’s not surprising that wildlife is flourishing, often quite close to human settlements or well-known tourist destinations like the Lake Balaton or the Hungarian Puszta. \"Wild Hungary\" is also the story of a fisherman and a herdsman for whom the rhythm of the river and the moving of the water makes the yearly calendar. \"Wild Hungary\" offers a view behind the clichés that lives about this country. And there are much more to taste than the famous goulash soup.","duration":3600000,"originalContentDuration":3105000,"allotment":3600,"rating":"All","featuredImage":{"path":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f859073a0a10014504ade/screenshot16_9.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=540&q=75&w=960"},"genre":"Documentary","type":"movie","seasonsNumbers":[],"stitched":{"path":"/stitch/hls/episode/626f859073a0a10014504ade/master.m3u8"},"covers":[{"aspectRatio":"347:500","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f859073a0a10014504ade/poster.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=1000&q=75&w=694"},{"aspectRatio":"4:3","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f859073a0a10014504ade/screenshot4_3.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=480&q=75&w=640"},{"aspectRatio":"16:9","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f859073a0a10014504ade/screenshot16_9.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=540&q=75&w=960"}],"categories":[{"id":"5b8d6316aff98879a8ee7157"}],"poster16_9":{"path":"https://images.pluto.tv/assets/images/default/vod.screenshot16_9-default.jpg"},"clip":{"actors":["Rob Quirk"],"directors":["Zoltán Török"],"writers":["Zoltán Török"],"producers":["Jörn Röver"],"originalReleaseDate":"2010-12-31T00:00:00Z"},"avail":{},"stream_url":"https://cfd-v4-service-channel-stitcher-use1-1.prd.pluto.tv/v2/stitch/hls/episode/626f859073a0a10014504ade/master.m3u8?advertisingId=&appName=web&appVersion=7.9.0-a9cca6b89aea4dc0998b92a51989d2adb9a9025d&app_name=web&clientDeviceType=0&clientID=688e2fcf-3b1e-4478-a146-7d2b26ed9b90&clientModelNumber=1.0.0&country=GB&deviceDNT=false&deviceId=688e2fcf-3b1e-4478-a146-7d2b26ed9b90&deviceLat=51.5100&deviceLon=-0.0800&deviceMake=Chrome&deviceModel=web&deviceType=web&deviceVersion=16.2.0&marketingRegion=GB&serverSideAds=true&sessionID=04ec44b2-d506-11f1-9e7f-2af1ca94ebdb&sid=04ec44b2-d506-11f1-9e7f-2af1ca94ebdb&userId=&jwt=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsImtpZCI6IjU3MGE4NTE5LTNhNzEtNGQ1Ni1iMTAyLTIwN2Q4MjI4MTZkYiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..12EU-uv7NlsyswTGY3ySL8nLtjjLm4qOFCmlC5Bnkno&masterJWTPassthrough=true"},"626f859a73a0a100145056ba-uk":{"_id":"626f859a73a0a100145056ba","seriesID":"626f859873a0a100145056b3","slug":"wild-berlin-2013-1-1","name":"Wild Berlin","summary":"Berlin is a European metropolis and home to millions of wild animals, living their lives in a fascinating parallel world as invisible companions, neighbors, sub letters or even friends.","description":"Berlin has a natural wild side - a fascinating parallel world of wildlife wonders great and small, right on the doorstep. For every human inhabitant of Berlin there are at least two birds, and nowhere else are so many sparrows and nightingales to be found as in Germany’s capital. Swarms of bees harvest the honey from the city’s almost half a million trees, while badgers can be found scurrying across courtyards and praying mantises await their prey in strips of railway land. The metropolis of Berlin is an urban jungle, providing a habitat for thousands of racoons, foxes, bats, squirrels, hedgehogs and beavers - Berlin is wild in more ways than one.","duration":3600000,"originalContentDuration":3120000,"allotment":3600,"rating":"All","featuredImage":{"path":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f859a73a0a100145056ba/screenshot16_9.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=540&q=75&w=960"},"genre":"Documentary","type":"movie","seasonsNumbers":[],"stitched":{"path":"/stitch/hls/episode/626f859a73a0a100145056ba/master.m3u8"},"covers":[{"aspectRatio":"347:500","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f859a73a0a100145056ba/poster.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=1000&q=75&w=694"},{"aspectRatio":"4:3","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f859a73a0a100145056ba/screenshot4_3.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=480&q=75&w=640"},{"aspectRatio":"16:9","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f859a73a0a100145056ba/screenshot16_9.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=540&q=75&w=960"}],"categories":[{"id":"5b8d6316aff98879a8ee7157"}],"poster16_9":{"path":"https://images.pluto.tv/assets/images/default/vod.screenshot16_9-default.jpg"},"clip":{"directors":["Rosi Koch","Roland Gockel"],"writers":["Rosi Koch","Roland Gockel"],"producers":["Dokfilm Fernsehproduktion GmbH"],"originalReleaseDate":"2013-12-31T00:00:00Z"},"avail":{},"stream_url":"https://cfd-v4-service-channel-stitcher-use1-1.prd.pluto.tv/v2/stitch/hls/episode/626f859a73a0a100145056ba/master.m3u8?advertisingId=&appName=web&appVersion=7.9.0-a9cca6b89aea4dc0998b92a51989d2adb9a9025d&app_name=web&clientDeviceType=0&clientID=688e2fcf-3b1e-4478-a146-7d2b26ed9b90&clientModelNumber=1.0.0&country=GB&deviceDNT=false&deviceId=688e2fcf-3b1e-4478-a146-7d2b26ed9b90&deviceLat=51.5100&deviceLon=-0.0800&deviceMake=Chrome&deviceModel=web&deviceType=web&deviceVersion=16.2.0&marketingRegion=GB&serverSideAds=true&sessionID=04ec44b2-d506-11f1-9e7f-2af1ca94ebdb&sid=04ec44b2-d506-11f1-9e7f-2af1ca94ebdb&userId=&jwt=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsImtpZCI6IjU3MGE4NTE5LTNhNzEtNGQ1Ni1iMTAyLTIwN2Q4MjI4MTZkYiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..12EU-uv7NlsyswTGY3ySL8nLtjjLm4qOFCmlC5Bnkno&masterJWTPassthrough=true"},"626f85ac73a0a10014506e0d-uk":{"_id":"626f85ac73a0a10014506e0d","seriesID":"626f85ab73a0a10014506e06","slug":"russias-hidden-paradises-2018-1-1","name":"Russia's Hidden Paradises","summary":"Russia is one of the most diverse and by far the largest country in the world. Its immense nature has always fascinated people.","description":"Russia is one of the most diverse and by far the largest country in the world. Its immense nature has always fascinated people. There are more than one hundred nature reserves, national parks and biosphere reserves between the lowlands in the west and the Mountains of fire on Kamchatka in the east. Dedicated researchers and nature conservationists fight daily to preserve this treasure. Four of these spectacular regions are representative of Russia's hidden paradises. The westernmost tip of Russia is the exclave of the Curonian Spit. A narrow strip of land that juts into the Baltic Sea. The Spit is a popular resting place for migratory birds on their journeys to the breeding grounds in the far north and to the winter quarters in the south. It is therefore not surprising that the oldest ornithological research station in the world has been observing the migration of birds here for more than a hundred years. Today, the most diverse migratory birds are briefly caught in gigantic traps made of fishing nets, examined for their state of health and ringed. Among other things, the data obtained provide researchers with clear evidence of global climate change. In the Far East on Kamchatka lies Lake Kuril, a paradise for the world's largest brown bears. At the time of the salmon migration they find food in abundance here. Since a dedicated anti-poaching unit has about 500 bears in sight, the furry giants are safe. Previously, poachers have repeatedly hunted the brown bears and served a flourishing market for bear products in China. High in the north in a desert of ice, live the reindeer herds of the Nenets. For centuries, the ungulates and the nomadic people have been well adapted to the hostile conditions on the Jamal peninsula. But despite all this flexibility, climate change and gas production are rapidly changing the world of the Nenets and their animals. In the south, the powerful and wild Caucasus borders the country.","duration":3000000,"originalContentDuration":2610000,"allotment":3000,"rating":"9+","featuredImage":{"path":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f85ac73a0a10014506e0d/screenshot16_9.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=540&q=75&w=960"},"genre":"Documentary","type":"movie","seasonsNumbers":[],"stitched":{"path":"/stitch/hls/episode/626f85ac73a0a10014506e0d/master.m3u8"},"covers":[{"aspectRatio":"347:500","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f85ac73a0a10014506e0d/poster.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=1000&q=75&w=694"},{"aspectRatio":"4:3","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f85ac73a0a10014506e0d/screenshot4_3.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=480&q=75&w=640"},{"aspectRatio":"16:9","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f85ac73a0a10014506e0d/screenshot16_9.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=540&q=75&w=960"}],"categories":[{"id":"5b8d6316aff98879a8ee7157"},{"id":"5c5bf751f21b553c1f673ad6"}],"poster16_9":{"path":"https://images.pluto.tv/assets/images/default/vod.screenshot16_9-default.jpg"},"clip":{"actors":["Nikita Chernetsov","Alexandra Sinelshikova","Albina Morilova","Sergej Shunorov","Anatolij Lasarenko","Ivan Guterev","Florian Stammler","Nikolai Khorotetto","Aurel Heidelberg","Valerii Shmunck"],"directors":["Iris Gesang"],"writers":["Iris Gesang"],"producers":["Kay Siering"],"originalReleaseDate":"2018-12-16T00:00:00Z"},"avail":{},"stream_url":"https://cfd-v4-service-channel-stitcher-use1-1.prd.pluto.tv/v2/stitch/hls/episode/626f85ac73a0a10014506e0d/master.m3u8?advertisingId=&appName=web&appVersion=7.9.0-a9cca6b89aea4dc0998b92a51989d2adb9a9025d&app_name=web&clientDeviceType=0&clientID=688e2fcf-3b1e-4478-a146-7d2b26ed9b90&clientModelNumber=1.0.0&country=GB&deviceDNT=false&deviceId=688e2fcf-3b1e-4478-a146-7d2b26ed9b90&deviceLat=51.5100&deviceLon=-0.0800&deviceMake=Chrome&deviceModel=web&deviceType=web&deviceVersion=16.2.0&marketingRegion=GB&serverSideAds=true&sessionID=04ec44b2-d506-11f1-9e7f-2af1ca94ebdb&sid=04ec44b2-d506-11f1-9e7f-2af1ca94ebdb&userId=&jwt=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsImtpZCI6IjU3MGE4NTE5LTNhNzEtNGQ1Ni1iMTAyLTIwN2Q4MjI4MTZkYiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..12EU-uv7NlsyswTGY3ySL8nLtjjLm4qOFCmlC5Bnkno&masterJWTPassthrough=true"},"626f85af73a0a1001450714a-uk":{"_id":"626f85af73a0a1001450714a","seriesID":"626f85ae73a0a10014507143","slug":"scandinavias-hidden-paradises-2019-1-1","name":"Scandinavia's Hidden Paradises","summary":"Four spectacular regions are representative of \"Scandinavia's hidden paradises\": High in the north, in Swedish Lapland, mighty moose feel at home.","description":"Scandinavia has always been a place of longing. Once covered by a kilometre-thick layer of ice, more than 100,000 years ago a mighty giant rose from the sea in the north of Europe, whose immense nature continues to fascinate people today. The Scandinavian Peninsula and the surrounding Nordic countries impress with numerous superlatives: the largest continental glacier, the deepest fjord in Europe, four UNESCO World Natural Heritage sites and more than 200,000 islands in Sweden alone. Dedicated researchers and nature conservationists fight daily to preserve this treasure. Four spectacular regions are representative of \"Scandinavia's hidden paradises\": High in the north, in Swedish Lapland, mighty moose feel at home. In winter, scientists mark individual animals with GPS collars to learn more about the migratory behaviour of Sweden's largest ungulate animal. Far to the east, in Finland, close to the Russian border, the vast Saimaa lake area is home to one of the rarest seal species in the world, the Saimaa ringed seal. There are only about 380 of them left. They are the last of their kind. Gotska Sandön is one of the most remote places in the southern island kingdom of the Baltic Sea, a paradise for birds and grey seals. Here scientists are looking for traces of settlements from past times. In the west, mountains and fjords dominate the landscape. Arctic foxes are once again living on the Norwegian plateau of Hallingskarvet. In all these places, conservationists are working with great enthusiasm for Scandinavia's hidden paradises.","duration":3000000,"originalContentDuration":2610000,"allotment":3000,"rating":"9+","featuredImage":{"path":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f85af73a0a1001450714a/screenshot16_9_1766613321007.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=540&q=75&w=960"},"genre":"Documentary","type":"movie","seasonsNumbers":[],"stitched":{"path":"/stitch/hls/episode/626f85af73a0a1001450714a/master.m3u8"},"covers":[{"aspectRatio":"347:500","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f85af73a0a1001450714a/poster_1766613321007.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=1000&q=75&w=694"},{"aspectRatio":"4:3","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f85af73a0a1001450714a/screenshot4_3_1766613321007.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=480&q=75&w=640"},{"aspectRatio":"16:9","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f85af73a0a1001450714a/screenshot16_9_1766613321007.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=540&q=75&w=960"}],"categories":[{"id":"5b8d6316aff98879a8ee7157"},{"id":"6422c9cf46622500082399df"}],"poster16_9":{"path":"https://images.pluto.tv/assets/images/default/vod.screenshot16_9-default.jpg"},"clip":{"actors":["Wiebke Neumann","Fredrik Stenbacka","Johan Rönnby","Sabine Sten","Ismo Marttinen","Meeri Koivuniemi","Petter Braaten","Kristoffer Ullern Hansen","Jacob Weigert"],"directors":["Anja Kindler","Iris Gesang"],"writers":["Anja Kindler","Iris Gesang"],"producers":["Kay Siering"],"originalReleaseDate":"2019-12-09T00:00:00Z"},"avail":{},"stream_url":"https://cfd-v4-service-channel-stitcher-use1-1.prd.pluto.tv/v2/stitch/hls/episode/626f85af73a0a1001450714a/master.m3u8?advertisingId=&appName=web&appVersion=7.9.0-a9cca6b89aea4dc0998b92a51989d2adb9a9025d&app_name=web&clientDeviceType=0&clientID=688e2fcf-3b1e-4478-a146-7d2b26ed9b90&clientModelNumber=1.0.0&country=GB&deviceDNT=false&deviceId=688e2fcf-3b1e-4478-a146-7d2b26ed9b90&deviceLat=51.5100&deviceLon=-0.0800&deviceMake=Chrome&deviceModel=web&deviceType=web&deviceVersion=16.2.0&marketingRegion=GB&serverSideAds=true&sessionID=04ec44b2-d506-11f1-9e7f-2af1ca94ebdb&sid=04ec44b2-d506-11f1-9e7f-2af1ca94ebdb&userId=&jwt=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsImtpZCI6IjU3MGE4NTE5LTNhNzEtNGQ1Ni1iMTAyLTIwN2Q4MjI4MTZkYiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..12EU-uv7NlsyswTGY3ySL8nLtjjLm4qOFCmlC5Bnkno&masterJWTPassthrough=true"},"5fa91cb5e5d584001a90dc87-uk":{"_id":"5fa91cb5e5d584001a90dc87","seriesID":"5fa91cb4e5d584001a90dc81","slug":"scotland-highlands-and-islands-2015-1-1","name":"Scotland - Highlands and Islands","summary":"An affectionate portrait of Scotland, with its unspoiled landscapes and unconventional inhabitants.","description":"Mysterious castles overlooking lonely lakes, and men in kilts playing the bagpipes; whiskey, and the Loch Ness monster: everybody is familiar with the clichés about Scotland. What few people realise, however, is that Great Britain‘s northernmost region also contains fascinating countryside and wildlife. Some of the biggest seabird colonies of Europe are in Scotland. The abundance of fish here also benefits the otters and ospreys who have returned to their Scottish hunting grounds in recent years. Spectacular aerial footage captures the beauty of the Highlands and some of the islands here: there are more than 500 of them in total. With the help of highly stabilised cameras and experienced pilots who have worked on the Harry Potter productions, we celebrate the overall charm of the Scottish landscape.","duration":3420000,"originalContentDuration":2895000,"allotment":3420,"rating":"All","featuredImage":{"path":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/5fa91cb5e5d584001a90dc87/screenshot16_9_1785868567151.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=540&q=75&w=960"},"genre":"Documentary","type":"movie","seasonsNumbers":[],"stitched":{"path":"/stitch/hls/episode/5fa91cb5e5d584001a90dc87/master.m3u8"},"covers":[{"aspectRatio":"347:500","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/5fa91cb5e5d584001a90dc87/poster_1785868567151.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=1000&q=75&w=694"},{"aspectRatio":"4:3","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/5fa91cb5e5d584001a90dc87/screenshot4_3_1785868567151.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=480&q=75&w=640"},{"aspectRatio":"16:9","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/5fa91cb5e5d584001a90dc87/screenshot16_9_1785868567151.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=540&q=75&w=960"}],"categories":[{"id":"5b8d6316aff98879a8ee7157"},{"id":"6422c9cf46622500082399df"}],"poster16_9":{"path":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/5fa91cb5e5d584001a90dc87/poster16_9_1785868567151.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=540&q=75&w=960"},"clip":{"actors":["Alistair Sutherland","Calum McInnan"],"directors":["Hans-Peter Kuttler","Ernst Sasse"],"writers":["Hans-Peter Kuttler","Ernst Sasse"],"producers":["Jörn Röver","Tom Synnatzschke"],"originalReleaseDate":"2015-07-10T00:00:00Z"},"avail":{},"stream_url":"https://cfd-v4-service-channel-stitcher-use1-1.prd.pluto.tv/v2/stitch/hls/episode/5fa91cb5e5d584001a90dc87/master.m3u8?advertisingId=&appName=web&appVersion=7.9.0-a9cca6b89aea4dc0998b92a51989d2adb9a9025d&app_name=web&clientDeviceType=0&clientID=688e2fcf-3b1e-4478-a146-7d2b26ed9b90&clientModelNumber=1.0.0&country=GB&deviceDNT=false&deviceId=688e2fcf-3b1e-4478-a146-7d2b26ed9b90&deviceLat=51.5100&deviceLon=-0.0800&deviceMake=Chrome&deviceModel=web&deviceType=web&deviceVersion=16.2.0&marketingRegion=GB&serverSideAds=true&sessionID=04ec44b2-d506-11f1-9e7f-2af1ca94ebdb&sid=04ec44b2-d506-11f1-9e7f-2af1ca94ebdb&userId=&jwt=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsImtpZCI6IjU3MGE4NTE5LTNhNzEtNGQ1Ni1iMTAyLTIwN2Q4MjI4MTZkYiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..12EU-uv7NlsyswTGY3ySL8nLtjjLm4qOFCmlC5Bnkno&masterJWTPassthrough=true"},"626f858d73a0a100145046de-uk":{"_id":"626f858d73a0a100145046de","seriesID":"626f858c73a0a100145046d7","slug":"the-antarctica-challenge-a-global-warning-2009-1-1","name":"The Antarctica Challenge - A Global Warning","summary":"Filmmaker Mark Terry leads an expedition to Antarctica to report on the discoveries made by the world’s scientific community stationed in Antarctica during International Polar Years.","description":"Filmmaker Mark Terry leads an expedition to Antarctica to report on the new discoveries made by the world’s scientific community stationed in Antarctica during International Polar Years (March, 2007 to March, 2009). This award-winning documentary will provide support interviews from polar experts and research scientists around the world as well as rare footage of wildlife. It reveals many startling new scientific revelations such as penguin suicide, new vegetation growing in the world’s largest desert, diminishing populations of land animals and marine life and the dangerously increasing melting of Antarctica’s land ice. These new discoveries were considered so valuable that this film became the only one invited by the United Nations tom screen to world leaders during the Climate Change Conference in Copenhagen, December, 2009.","duration":3660000,"originalContentDuration":3135000,"allotment":3660,"rating":"9+","featuredImage":{"path":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f858d73a0a100145046de/screenshot16_9_1786058650799.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=540&q=75&w=960"},"genre":"Documentary","type":"movie","seasonsNumbers":[],"stitched":{"path":"/stitch/hls/episode/626f858d73a0a100145046de/master.m3u8"},"covers":[{"aspectRatio":"347:500","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f858d73a0a100145046de/poster_1786058650799.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=1000&q=75&w=694"},{"aspectRatio":"4:3","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f858d73a0a100145046de/screenshot4_3_1786058650799.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=480&q=75&w=640"},{"aspectRatio":"16:9","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f858d73a0a100145046de/screenshot16_9_1786058650799.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=540&q=75&w=960"}],"categories":[{"id":"5b8d6316aff98879a8ee7157"}],"poster16_9":{"path":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f858d73a0a100145046de/poster16_9_1786058650799.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=540&q=75&w=960"},"clip":{"directors":["Mark Terry"],"writers":["Mark Terry"],"producers":["Mark Terry"],"originalReleaseDate":"2009-06-07T00:00:00Z"},"avail":{},"stream_url":"https://cfd-v4-service-channel-stitcher-use1-1.prd.pluto.tv/v2/stitch/hls/episode/626f858d73a0a100145046de/master.m3u8?advertisingId=&appName=web&appVersion=7.9.0-a9cca6b89aea4dc0998b92a51989d2adb9a9025d&app_name=web&clientDeviceType=0&clientID=688e2fcf-3b1e-4478-a146-7d2b26ed9b90&clientModelNumber=1.0.0&country=GB&deviceDNT=false&deviceId=688e2fcf-3b1e-4478-a146-7d2b26ed9b90&deviceLat=51.5100&deviceLon=-0.0800&deviceMake=Chrome&deviceModel=web&deviceType=web&deviceVersion=16.2.0&marketingRegion=GB&serverSideAds=true&sessionID=04ec44b2-d506-11f1-9e7f-2af1ca94ebdb&sid=04ec44b2-d506-11f1-9e7f-2af1ca94ebdb&userId=&jwt=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsImtpZCI6IjU3MGE4NTE5LTNhNzEtNGQ1Ni1iMTAyLTIwN2Q4MjI4MTZkYiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..12EU-uv7NlsyswTGY3ySL8nLtjjLm4qOFCmlC5Bnkno&masterJWTPassthrough=true"},"6017b96e5777bb001aa9ea11-uk":{"_id":"6017b96e5777bb001aa9ea11","seriesID":"6017b96d5777bb001aa9ea0b","slug":"bitter-seeds-2010-1-1","name":"Bitter Seeds","summary":"Bitter Seeds explores the future of how we grow things. The worldwide debate focuses on how farming is being drastically transformed by the demands of industrial agriculture.","description":"Bitter Seeds explores the future of how we grow things. The worldwide debate focuses on how farming is being drastically transformed by the demands of industrial agriculture.","duration":5760000,"originalContentDuration":5100000,"allotment":5760,"rating":"9+","featuredImage":{"path":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/6017b96e5777bb001aa9ea11/screenshot16_9_1785774961188.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=540&q=75&w=960"},"genre":"Documentary","type":"movie","seasonsNumbers":[],"stitched":{"path":"/stitch/hls/episode/6017b96e5777bb001aa9ea11/master.m3u8"},"covers":[{"aspectRatio":"347:500","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/6017b96e5777bb001aa9ea11/poster_1785774961188.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=1000&q=75&w=694"},{"aspectRatio":"4:3","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/6017b96e5777bb001aa9ea11/screenshot4_3_1785774961188.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=480&q=75&w=640"},{"aspectRatio":"16:9","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/6017b96e5777bb001aa9ea11/screenshot16_9_1785774961188.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=540&q=75&w=960"}],"categories":[{"id":"5b8d6316aff98879a8ee7157"}],"poster16_9":{"path":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/6017b96e5777bb001aa9ea11/poster16_9_1785774961188.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=540&q=75&w=960"},"clip":{"originalReleaseDate":"2011-01-01T00:00:00Z"},"avail":{},"stream_url":"https://cfd-v4-service-channel-stitcher-use1-1.prd.pluto.tv/v2/stitch/hls/episode/6017b96e5777bb001aa9ea11/master.m3u8?advertisingId=&appName=web&appVersion=7.9.0-a9cca6b89aea4dc0998b92a51989d2adb9a9025d&app_name=web&clientDeviceType=0&clientID=688e2fcf-3b1e-4478-a146-7d2b26ed9b90&clientModelNumber=1.0.0&country=GB&deviceDNT=false&deviceId=688e2fcf-3b1e-4478-a146-7d2b26ed9b90&deviceLat=51.5100&deviceLon=-0.0800&deviceMake=Chrome&deviceModel=web&deviceType=web&deviceVersion=16.2.0&marketingRegion=GB&serverSideAds=true&sessionID=04ec44b2-d506-11f1-9e7f-2af1ca94ebdb&sid=04ec44b2-d506-11f1-9e7f-2af1ca94ebdb&userId=&jwt=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsImtpZCI6IjU3MGE4NTE5LTNhNzEtNGQ1Ni1iMTAyLTIwN2Q4MjI4MTZkYiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..12EU-uv7NlsyswTGY3ySL8nLtjjLm4qOFCmlC5Bnkno&masterJWTPassthrough=true"},"5fa91ccae5d584001a90de24-uk":{"_id":"5fa91ccae5d584001a90de24","seriesID":"5fa91cc9e5d584001a90de1e","slug":"urban-jungle-2016-1-1","name":"Urban Jungle","summary":"The concrete jungle’s teaming with animals, but how do these city-slickers get by in the Urban Jungle?","description":"We think cities belong to us, but the concrete jungle’s teaming with animals - whether its monkeys in Japan, sparrows in Germany, Turkish rats or even Manatee in Florida. We make friends with some, but most go about their lives unseen. Some people see wild animals as pests, and dangerous to our health, others believe they are crucial to our well-being and belong here as much as we do. What is the truth about these street-smart city-slickers, and how do they get by in the Urban Jungle? All over the world, human populations are rapidly expanding, numbering more than 7 billion globally. And as our populations increase so does the spread of concrete. Urban sprawl to house ever more people. Whether it’s a small town or a vast city, we think of the urban jungle as human habitat, but look closer - we are not the only ones who are street smart. Cities have been built in rich habitats because they suited our needs - but for the same reasons we are attracted to the locations, animals are too. And just as we adapt to an ever more urban environment, so do they. There’s evidence that song birds sing as different frequencies in the city to be heard over traffic. Squirrels have given up trying to shout over the noise and instead communicate with each other through body language. And it’s even thought that mice and voles might have bigger brains in cities because they need to think fast to survive the rat race. People don’t always embrace urban wildlife, but we benefit from them in many ways; Bats and wasps control the numbers of insects that would bite us or damage our property, foxes and birds of prey help to control populations of rodents, pigeons and other creatures we consider pests, and of course bees and butterflies pollinate plants.","duration":3540000,"originalContentDuration":3000000,"allotment":3540,"rating":"9+","featuredImage":{"path":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/5fa91ccae5d584001a90de24/screenshot16_9_1789580882087.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=540&q=75&w=960"},"genre":"Documentary","type":"movie","seasonsNumbers":[],"stitched":{"path":"/stitch/hls/episode/5fa91ccae5d584001a90de24/master.m3u8"},"covers":[{"aspectRatio":"347:500","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/5fa91ccae5d584001a90de24/poster_1789580882087.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=1000&q=75&w=694"},{"aspectRatio":"4:3","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/5fa91ccae5d584001a90de24/screenshot4_3_1789580882087.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=480&q=75&w=640"},{"aspectRatio":"16:9","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/5fa91ccae5d584001a90de24/screenshot16_9_1789580882087.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=540&q=75&w=960"}],"categories":[{"id":"5b8d6316aff98879a8ee7157"}],"poster16_9":{"path":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/5fa91ccae5d584001a90de24/poster16_9_1789580882087.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=540&q=75&w=960"},"clip":{"actors":["Andy Wisher"],"directors":["Phil Coles"],"producers":["Tom Synnatzschke"],"originalReleaseDate":"2016-12-30T00:00:00Z"},"avail":{},"stream_url":"https://cfd-v4-service-channel-stitcher-use1-1.prd.pluto.tv/v2/stitch/hls/episode/5fa91ccae5d584001a90de24/master.m3u8?advertisingId=&appName=web&appVersion=7.9.0-a9cca6b89aea4dc0998b92a51989d2adb9a9025d&app_name=web&clientDeviceType=0&clientID=688e2fcf-3b1e-4478-a146-7d2b26ed9b90&clientModelNumber=1.0.0&country=GB&deviceDNT=false&deviceId=688e2fcf-3b1e-4478-a146-7d2b26ed9b90&deviceLat=51.5100&deviceLon=-0.0800&deviceMake=Chrome&deviceModel=web&deviceType=web&deviceVersion=16.2.0&marketingRegion=GB&serverSideAds=true&sessionID=04ec44b2-d506-11f1-9e7f-2af1ca94ebdb&sid=04ec44b2-d506-11f1-9e7f-2af1ca94ebdb&userId=&jwt=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsImtpZCI6IjU3MGE4NTE5LTNhNzEtNGQ1Ni1iMTAyLTIwN2Q4MjI4MTZkYiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..12EU-uv7NlsyswTGY3ySL8nLtjjLm4qOFCmlC5Bnkno&masterJWTPassthrough=true"},"5fa91cd7e5d584001a90df17-uk":{"_id":"5fa91cd7e5d584001a90df17","seriesID":"5fa91cd7e5d584001a90df11","slug":"the-lesser-caucasus-between-ararat-and-the-caspian-sea-2013-1-1","name":"The Lesser Caucasus - Between Ararat and the Caspian Sea","summary":"Armenia, Georgia and Azerbaijan: in this impressive documentary, we present the exceptional nature and landscape diversity of the lesser Caucasus.","description":"The mountain worlds of the Greater and Lesser Caucasus mark the border between Europe and Asia. After their documentary about the Greater Caucasus, Henry J. Mix and his team have now prepared a second film about the impressive mountain world of this region. The species and landscape diversity of the lesser Caucasus are portrayed in Armenia, Georgia and Azerbaijan. Shielded from the more than 4000-metre-tall main ridge of the Greater Caucasus, a thermophilic flora and fauna was able to develop in the Lesser Caucasus. For the first time, the astonishing variety of the land bridge between Europe and Persia is portrayed comprehensively. From the mountains of Dagestan, down to the canyons of the Caspian Basin, through the steppes of Azerbaijan and up into the Armenian highlands, all before the majestic backdrop of biblical Mount Ararat.","duration":3420000,"originalContentDuration":2910000,"allotment":3420,"rating":"9+","featuredImage":{"path":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/5fa91cd7e5d584001a90df17/screenshot16_9.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=540&q=75&w=960"},"genre":"Documentary","type":"movie","seasonsNumbers":[],"stitched":{"path":"/stitch/hls/episode/5fa91cd7e5d584001a90df17/master.m3u8"},"covers":[{"aspectRatio":"347:500","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/5fa91cd7e5d584001a90df17/poster.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=1000&q=75&w=694"},{"aspectRatio":"4:3","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/5fa91cd7e5d584001a90df17/screenshot4_3.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=480&q=75&w=640"},{"aspectRatio":"16:9","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/5fa91cd7e5d584001a90df17/screenshot16_9.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=540&q=75&w=960"}],"categories":[{"id":"5b8d6316aff98879a8ee7157"},{"id":"5c5bf751f21b553c1f673ad6"}],"poster16_9":{"path":"https://images.pluto.tv/assets/images/default/vod.screenshot16_9-default.jpg"},"clip":{"directors":["Henry M. Mix"],"writers":["Henry M. Mix"],"producers":["Tom Synnatzschke","Jörn Röver"],"originalReleaseDate":"2013-12-30T00:00:00Z"},"avail":{},"stream_url":"https://cfd-v4-service-channel-stitcher-use1-1.prd.pluto.tv/v2/stitch/hls/episode/5fa91cd7e5d584001a90df17/master.m3u8?advertisingId=&appName=web&appVersion=7.9.0-a9cca6b89aea4dc0998b92a51989d2adb9a9025d&app_name=web&clientDeviceType=0&clientID=688e2fcf-3b1e-4478-a146-7d2b26ed9b90&clientModelNumber=1.0.0&country=GB&deviceDNT=false&deviceId=688e2fcf-3b1e-4478-a146-7d2b26ed9b90&deviceLat=51.5100&deviceLon=-0.0800&deviceMake=Chrome&deviceModel=web&deviceType=web&deviceVersion=16.2.0&marketingRegion=GB&serverSideAds=true&sessionID=04ec44b2-d506-11f1-9e7f-2af1ca94ebdb&sid=04ec44b2-d506-11f1-9e7f-2af1ca94ebdb&userId=&jwt=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsImtpZCI6IjU3MGE4NTE5LTNhNzEtNGQ1Ni1iMTAyLTIwN2Q4MjI4MTZkYiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..12EU-uv7NlsyswTGY3ySL8nLtjjLm4qOFCmlC5Bnkno&masterJWTPassthrough=true"},"5fa91cd6e5d584001a90df00-uk":{"_id":"5fa91cd6e5d584001a90df00","seriesID":"5fa91cd5e5d584001a90defa","slug":"the-greater-caucasus-2013-1-1","name":"The Greater Caucasus","summary":"The last mountain bison, Caucasian ibexes, craggy peaks and extreme weather fluctuations - an impressive nature documentary was filmed in the immediate hinterland of Sochi.","description":"The mountains of the Caucasus form a magical border between Europe and Asia. Film-maker Henry M. Mix and his crew spent over a year in Russia's highest mountains. The result is an impressive documentary about the natural wonders to be found between the Black and Caspian Seas. The wild mountain landscape with its extreme climate has created a unique world of flora and fauna and makes the Caucasus one of the world's 25 most significant centres of biodiversity. Mountain bison, Caucasus Snowcock and tur are only found here. In the rain shadow of the snow-covered main ridge live Saiga antelopes, long-eared hedgehogs and short-toed snake eagles. Epic footage, breath-taking aerial photography and hitherto unseen behaviour of rare animals - Greater Caucasus has its viewers spellbound from the first minute on.","duration":3480000,"originalContentDuration":2970000,"allotment":3480,"rating":"9+","featuredImage":{"path":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/5fa91cd6e5d584001a90df00/screenshot16_9_1790967604776.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=540&q=75&w=960"},"genre":"Documentary","type":"movie","seasonsNumbers":[],"stitched":{"path":"/stitch/hls/episode/5fa91cd6e5d584001a90df00/master.m3u8"},"covers":[{"aspectRatio":"347:500","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/5fa91cd6e5d584001a90df00/poster_1790967604776.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=1000&q=75&w=694"},{"aspectRatio":"4:3","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/5fa91cd6e5d584001a90df00/screenshot4_3_1790967604776.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=480&q=75&w=640"},{"aspectRatio":"16:9","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/5fa91cd6e5d584001a90df00/screenshot16_9_1790967604776.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=540&q=75&w=960"}],"categories":[{"id":"5b8d6316aff98879a8ee7157"}],"poster16_9":{"path":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/5fa91cd6e5d584001a90df00/poster16_9_1790967604776.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=540&q=75&w=960"},"clip":{"directors":["Henry M. Mix"],"writers":["Henry M. Mix"],"producers":["Jörn Röver","Tom Synnatzschke"],"originalReleaseDate":"2013-12-30T00:00:00Z"},"avail":{},"stream_url":"https://cfd-v4-service-channel-stitcher-use1-1.prd.pluto.tv/v2/stitch/hls/episode/5fa91cd6e5d584001a90df00/master.m3u8?advertisingId=&appName=web&appVersion=7.9.0-a9cca6b89aea4dc0998b92a51989d2adb9a9025d&app_name=web&clientDeviceType=0&clientID=688e2fcf-3b1e-4478-a146-7d2b26ed9b90&clientModelNumber=1.0.0&country=GB&deviceDNT=false&deviceId=688e2fcf-3b1e-4478-a146-7d2b26ed9b90&deviceLat=51.5100&deviceLon=-0.0800&deviceMake=Chrome&deviceModel=web&deviceType=web&deviceVersion=16.2.0&marketingRegion=GB&serverSideAds=true&sessionID=04ec44b2-d506-11f1-9e7f-2af1ca94ebdb&sid=04ec44b2-d506-11f1-9e7f-2af1ca94ebdb&userId=&jwt=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsImtpZCI6IjU3MGE4NTE5LTNhNzEtNGQ1Ni1iMTAyLTIwN2Q4MjI4MTZkYiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..12EU-uv7NlsyswTGY3ySL8nLtjjLm4qOFCmlC5Bnkno&masterJWTPassthrough=true"},"626f85c073a0a100145084fe-uk":{"_id":"626f85c073a0a100145084fe","seriesID":"626f85be73a0a100145084f7","slug":"global-forest-2015-1-1","name":"Global Forest","summary":"Trees cover 4 billion hectares of our planet. It’s one of the most vibrant landscapes that changes constantly throughout the year.","description":"Trees cover 4 billion hectares of our planet, a vast blanket of green that produces a third of the Earths oxygen essential to all life. It’s one of the most vibrant landscapes that changes constantly throughout the year. Stretching well into the northern territories, it sees hot summers and harsh cold winters, but provides sanctuary to a glorious and diverse array of animal life. Some animals use the forests only during the rich summer months, and fly south or curl up and sleep to avoid the worst of the weather, but there are many species that use the forest year round. For those creatures, the bears, wolves, moose, foxes, lynx and deer winters can be terrible hard; they must scrape snow and make the most of the tiniest scraps of food, but it’s worth it when spring sun brings on the fresh growth and transforms the lush forest.","duration":3540000,"originalContentDuration":3015000,"allotment":3540,"rating":"9+","featuredImage":{"path":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f85c073a0a100145084fe/screenshot16_9_1786393801238.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=540&q=75&w=960"},"genre":"Documentary","type":"movie","seasonsNumbers":[],"stitched":{"path":"/stitch/hls/episode/626f85c073a0a100145084fe/master.m3u8"},"covers":[{"aspectRatio":"347:500","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f85c073a0a100145084fe/poster_1786393801238.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=1000&q=75&w=694"},{"aspectRatio":"4:3","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f85c073a0a100145084fe/screenshot4_3_1786393801238.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=480&q=75&w=640"},{"aspectRatio":"16:9","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f85c073a0a100145084fe/screenshot16_9_1786393801238.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=540&q=75&w=960"}],"categories":[{"id":"5b8d6316aff98879a8ee7157"}],"poster16_9":{"path":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f85c073a0a100145084fe/poster16_9_1786393801238.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=540&q=75&w=960"},"clip":{"actors":["Andy Wisher"],"directors":["Phil Coles"],"writers":["Phil Coles"],"producers":["Phil Coles"],"originalReleaseDate":"2015-11-30T00:00:00Z"},"avail":{},"stream_url":"https://cfd-v4-service-channel-stitcher-use1-1.prd.pluto.tv/v2/stitch/hls/episode/626f85c073a0a100145084fe/master.m3u8?advertisingId=&appName=web&appVersion=7.9.0-a9cca6b89aea4dc0998b92a51989d2adb9a9025d&app_name=web&clientDeviceType=0&clientID=688e2fcf-3b1e-4478-a146-7d2b26ed9b90&clientModelNumber=1.0.0&country=GB&deviceDNT=false&deviceId=688e2fcf-3b1e-4478-a146-7d2b26ed9b90&deviceLat=51.5100&deviceLon=-0.0800&deviceMake=Chrome&deviceModel=web&deviceType=web&deviceVersion=16.2.0&marketingRegion=GB&serverSideAds=true&sessionID=04ec44b2-d506-11f1-9e7f-2af1ca94ebdb&sid=04ec44b2-d506-11f1-9e7f-2af1ca94ebdb&userId=&jwt=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsImtpZCI6IjU3MGE4NTE5LTNhNzEtNGQ1Ni1iMTAyLTIwN2Q4MjI4MTZkYiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..12EU-uv7NlsyswTGY3ySL8nLtjjLm4qOFCmlC5Bnkno&masterJWTPassthrough=true"},"626f85a673a0a1001450662f-uk":{"_id":"626f85a673a0a1001450662f","seriesID":"626f85a573a0a10014506628","slug":"forest-of-heroes-2021-1-1","name":"Forest of Heroes","summary":"One of Germany’s most beautiful and mysterious forests - the Teutoburg Forest.","description":"From Lower Saxony and North Rhine Westphalia, from Osnabrück to Paderborn, one of Germany’s most beautiful forests extends for some 150 kilometers - the Teutoburg Forest. The low mountain range became famous due to the Varus Battle that took place in 9 AD. It was here that Hermann, or Arminius, the Cherusci Prince vanquished the Roman occupation army. His monument near Detmold is still the most important landmark of the Teutoburg Forest. But there is even more nature in and around the shadow cast by Hermann. And now, the forest once so dreaded by the Romans, is now known for its unspoiled nature. The dense, tall shrubs on the ridge are home to boars and red deer, dormice and common toads - a valuable forest and a unique habitat. During the damp and windless winter nights, one can experience a rare phenomenon at the Extern Stones: threads of ice seemingly grow out of the deadwood. As thin as hair, in just one night they can grow up to 20 centimetres! In the Wistinghaus Senne, there are even animal forest managers. On behalf of a nature preservation project, Exmoor ponies and Scottish Highland cattle were settled in order to keep the forest in check. At the same time they create open spaces, which are important for other animals, such as the red-backed shrike. In the often more than 100-year-old beech trees, the black woodpecker finds more than enough space to hammer out a hollow in the wood. This usually takes around one month to complete. The woodpecker has to hack at the wood 17 times until one single woodchip becomes loose. This works out as more than 10,000 chips until the nest is complete. During the two years spent filming, nature film makers Svenja and Ralph Schieke were able to document the Teutoburg Forest intensively. The impressive dynamics of the forest are relayed to us via time lapse and seasons-morphing. Remote-controlled drones enable fascinating views of the unique forest landscape.","duration":3540000,"originalContentDuration":3030000,"allotment":3540,"rating":"9+","featuredImage":{"path":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f85a673a0a1001450662f/screenshot16_9_1786129202856.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=540&q=75&w=960"},"genre":"Documentary","type":"movie","seasonsNumbers":[],"stitched":{"path":"/stitch/hls/episode/626f85a673a0a1001450662f/master.m3u8"},"covers":[{"aspectRatio":"347:500","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f85a673a0a1001450662f/poster_1786129202856.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=1000&q=75&w=694"},{"aspectRatio":"4:3","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f85a673a0a1001450662f/screenshot4_3_1786129202856.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=480&q=75&w=640"},{"aspectRatio":"16:9","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f85a673a0a1001450662f/screenshot16_9_1786129202856.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=540&q=75&w=960"}],"categories":[{"id":"5b8d6316aff98879a8ee7157"}],"poster16_9":{"path":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f85a673a0a1001450662f/poster16_9_1786129202856.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=540&q=75&w=960"},"clip":{"actors":["Colin Solman"],"directors":["Svenja Schieke","Ralph Schieke"],"writers":["Svenja Schieke","Ralph Schieke"],"producers":["Simon Riedel"],"originalReleaseDate":"2021-04-06T00:00:00Z"},"avail":{},"stream_url":"https://cfd-v4-service-channel-stitcher-use1-1.prd.pluto.tv/v2/stitch/hls/episode/626f85a673a0a1001450662f/master.m3u8?advertisingId=&appName=web&appVersion=7.9.0-a9cca6b89aea4dc0998b92a51989d2adb9a9025d&app_name=web&clientDeviceType=0&clientID=688e2fcf-3b1e-4478-a146-7d2b26ed9b90&clientModelNumber=1.0.0&country=GB&deviceDNT=false&deviceId=688e2fcf-3b1e-4478-a146-7d2b26ed9b90&deviceLat=51.5100&deviceLon=-0.0800&deviceMake=Chrome&deviceModel=web&deviceType=web&deviceVersion=16.2.0&marketingRegion=GB&serverSideAds=true&sessionID=04ec44b2-d506-11f1-9e7f-2af1ca94ebdb&sid=04ec44b2-d506-11f1-9e7f-2af1ca94ebdb&userId=&jwt=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsImtpZCI6IjU3MGE4NTE5LTNhNzEtNGQ1Ni1iMTAyLTIwN2Q4MjI4MTZkYiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..12EU-uv7NlsyswTGY3ySL8nLtjjLm4qOFCmlC5Bnkno&masterJWTPassthrough=true"},"626f85bc73a0a100145080ef-uk":{"_id":"626f85bc73a0a100145080ef","seriesID":"626f85bb73a0a100145080e8","slug":"born-to-fly-2015-1-1","name":"Born to Fly","summary":"We envy birds their mastery of the air, watching them enjoy the freedom of a 3 dimensional space.","description":"We envy birds, watching them enjoy the freedom of a 3 dimensional space. Flight allows them to get to hard to reach places and preform aerial acrobatics in protecting home ranges and searching for food. But it’s not always easy – it takes a lot of effort to graduate air school and there is a new bunch of cadets arriving all hoping to get their wings. Thanks to their flying skills birds can go anywhere, often undertaking huge migrations. The Arctic tern is one bird that can even fly from pole to pole. But birds don’t come out of an egg ready to programmed for the air. Parent birds work tirelessly to nurture and train their young. As they get older the chicks start spreading their wings and experimenting with flight. Before long they can join their parents in the skies. All we can do it watch in awe and wish we could join them.","duration":3540000,"originalContentDuration":3015000,"allotment":3540,"rating":"9+","featuredImage":{"path":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f85bc73a0a100145080ef/screenshot16_9.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=540&q=75&w=960"},"genre":"Documentary","type":"movie","seasonsNumbers":[],"stitched":{"path":"/stitch/hls/episode/626f85bc73a0a100145080ef/master.m3u8"},"covers":[{"aspectRatio":"347:500","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f85bc73a0a100145080ef/poster.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=1000&q=75&w=694"},{"aspectRatio":"4:3","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f85bc73a0a100145080ef/screenshot4_3.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=480&q=75&w=640"},{"aspectRatio":"16:9","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f85bc73a0a100145080ef/screenshot16_9.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=540&q=75&w=960"}],"categories":[{"id":"5b8d6316aff98879a8ee7157"}],"poster16_9":{"path":"https://images.pluto.tv/assets/images/default/vod.screenshot16_9-default.jpg"},"clip":{"actors":["Andy Wisher"],"directors":["Phil Coles"],"writers":["Phil Coles"],"producers":["Phil Coles"],"originalReleaseDate":"2015-11-30T00:00:00Z"},"avail":{},"stream_url":"https://cfd-v4-service-channel-stitcher-use1-1.prd.pluto.tv/v2/stitch/hls/episode/626f85bc73a0a100145080ef/master.m3u8?advertisingId=&appName=web&appVersion=7.9.0-a9cca6b89aea4dc0998b92a51989d2adb9a9025d&app_name=web&clientDeviceType=0&clientID=688e2fcf-3b1e-4478-a146-7d2b26ed9b90&clientModelNumber=1.0.0&country=GB&deviceDNT=false&deviceId=688e2fcf-3b1e-4478-a146-7d2b26ed9b90&deviceLat=51.5100&deviceLon=-0.0800&deviceMake=Chrome&deviceModel=web&deviceType=web&deviceVersion=16.2.0&marketingRegion=GB&serverSideAds=true&sessionID=04ec44b2-d506-11f1-9e7f-2af1ca94ebdb&sid=04ec44b2-d506-11f1-9e7f-2af1ca94ebdb&userId=&jwt=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsImtpZCI6IjU3MGE4NTE5LTNhNzEtNGQ1Ni1iMTAyLTIwN2Q4MjI4MTZkYiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..12EU-uv7NlsyswTGY3ySL8nLtjjLm4qOFCmlC5Bnkno&masterJWTPassthrough=true"},"626f858a73a0a10014503ff3-uk":{"_id":"626f858a73a0a10014503ff3","seriesID":"626f858873a0a10014503fec","slug":"adventure-ocean-quest-special-2019-1-1","name":"Adventure Ocean Quest - Special","summary":"The famous underwater cameraman Christian Petron accompanies the former world champion in freediving, Frederic Buyle, with its exciting diving without breathing apparatus.","description":"Adventure Ocean Quest: the documentary is showing stunning wildlife- and nature images exciting adventures and fascinating encounters between humans and marine life: A 90-minute dive adventure, developed by the Wiesbaden located film production company Sound & Vision together with the renowned French underwater filmmaker Christian Petron. Unlike previous underwater documentaries this expedition opens a new gateway to \"the realm of depth\": The famous underwater cameraman Christian Petron accompanies the former world champion in freediving, Frederic Buyle, with its exciting diving without breathing apparatus. Freedivers are \"water people\" who move silently and elegantly underwater. Frederic Buyle emerges without air tanks to depths of over 50 meters and stays there for several minutes. He uses his impressive skills to the \"soft inquiry\" of marine animals and their behavior. His ability allows him to approach the inhabitants of the ocean, without disturbing it - unlike normal divers whose diving equipment causing loud breathing noises and clouds of bubbles. The team also waived the usual \"bait\" or lures to observe only realistic and lifelike behavior of animals. In his dives Frederic receives exclusive recordings from the natural behavior of wild animals. In his collaboration with scientists creating new reliable portraits of many already known species. Christian Petron documented with masterful and extraordinary images marked by respect and honor these encounters between humans and marine life.","duration":6240000,"originalContentDuration":5430000,"allotment":6240,"rating":"9+","featuredImage":{"path":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f858a73a0a10014503ff3/screenshot16_9.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=540&q=75&w=960"},"genre":"Documentary","type":"movie","seasonsNumbers":[],"stitched":{"path":"/stitch/hls/episode/626f858a73a0a10014503ff3/master.m3u8"},"covers":[{"aspectRatio":"347:500","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f858a73a0a10014503ff3/poster.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=1000&q=75&w=694"},{"aspectRatio":"4:3","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f858a73a0a10014503ff3/screenshot4_3.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=480&q=75&w=640"},{"aspectRatio":"16:9","url":"https://images.pluto.tv/episodes/626f858a73a0a10014503ff3/screenshot16_9.jpg?fill=blur&fit=fill&fm=jpg&h=540&q=75&w=960"}],"categories":[{"id":"5b8d6316aff98879a8ee7157"}],"poster16_9":{"path":"https://images.pluto.tv/assets/images/default/vod.screenshot16_9-default.jpg"},"clip":{"actors":["Frédéric Bulye","William Winram","Pierre Frolla"],"directors":["Christian Petron","Boris Raim"],"writers":["Christian Petron","Boris Raim"],"producers":["Sound & Vision GmbH"],"originalReleaseDate":"2019-03-03T00:00:00Z"},"avail":{},"stream_url":"https://cfd-v4-service-channel-stitcher-use1-1.prd.pluto.tv/v2/stitch/hls/episode/626f858a73a0a1001